<div class="mw-parser-output"><h1>Terminal</h1>
<p>Usage:
</p>
<pre>change terminal dumb
change terminal tty
change terminal ansi
change telnet
</pre>
<p>These settings matter only when you play over telnet or with a mud 
client such as Mudlet or TinTin++; the web client looks after them for 
you.
</p><p><b>change terminal</b> tells the game what your screen understands: 
<b>ansi</b> for colours, which nearly every client and terminal can show; 
<b>tty</b> for a plain terminal; <b>dumb</b> for no special codes at all. 
If you see garbage characters instead of words, or no colours, try 
another setting.
</p><p><b>change telnet</b> switches whether the game assumes you use a telnet 
program, which lets it, for example, hide your password as you type it. 
Turn it off only if your client prints odd characters after each line.
</p><p>Your settings are kept with your character.
</p><p><br />
See Also:
</p>
<pre>&gt; <a cmd='#'>Help Change</a>
&gt; <a cmd='#'>Help Columns</a>
</pre>




</div>